sentences.text:
During pendency of the said appeals, the petitioners filed an Interlocutory Application vide I.A. Nos.476 and 477 of 2024 in the said appeals under Order - XVII,
Rule -1 read with 151 of CPC to adjourn the said appeals for at least three months or till FSL report is received contending as follows:
i) Respondent No.2 is claiming that he purchased the suit schedule properties from respondent No.1 under a registered sale deed;
KL,J CRP Nos.2529 & 2530 of 2024 H. Veeramallu vs H. Komuraiah on 14 August, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/88840434/
1 ii) Respondent No.1 claimed the suit schedule properties on the strength of Ex.B1 - alleged unregistered partition deeds, both dated 10.03.1998;
iii) The petitioners' claim is that deceased petitioner No.1 never signed on Ex.B1 - alleged partition deed and that the signature of deceased petitioner No.1 was forged by respondent No.1.

iv) The petitioners filed a protest petition vide Crl.M.P. No.282 of 2024 and thereafter, vide official memorandum dated 21.05.2024, learned Special Judicial Magistrate of First Class (Excise),
Karimnagar, directed the Investigating Officer to collect and send Ex.B1 along with admitted signature available on pattadar passbook of KL,J CRP Nos.2529 & 2530 of 2024 the deceased petitioner No.1 to FSL, Hyderabad for comparison and report;
v) The said FSL report is awaiting.
